# Strix (usestrix/strix) — open-source AI pentesting CLI.
# Standalone tool: reads plain env vars at `strix` invocation time, NOT part of
# apps/backend ConfigService. Docs: https://docs.strix.ai/advanced/configuration
#
# Policy for this repo: only local models and GLM (z.ai) are approved LLM backends
# for Strix — no OpenAI/Anthropic/Google, since scans read this codebase (HR/PII
# domain, see CLAUDE.md §Критические правила). Pick ONE profile below.
#
# Usage:
#   cp infra/scripts/security/.env.strix.example infra/scripts/security/.env.strix
#   set -a && source infra/scripts/security/.env.strix && set +a
#   strix -n -t ./ --scan-mode quick --max-budget 5

# --- Profile A: local Ollama (default) — quick/standard scans, zero cost, nothing leaves the machine ---
# Same alias the backend agent pipeline uses — see apps/backend/.env.example OLLAMA_MODEL_AGENT
# and infra/scripts/dev-ai/ollama-setup-agent-pipeline.sh (npm run ollama:pipeline).
# Requires `ollama serve` running locally with the hr-helper-agent alias already pulled.
STRIX_LLM=ollama/hr-helper-agent
LLM_API_BASE=http://127.0.0.1:11434

# --- Profile B: GLM via z.ai API (deep/full scan) — stronger reasoning, use for --scan-mode deep ---
# To switch: comment out Profile A above, uncomment these three lines.
# Reuses ZAI_API_KEY from apps/backend/.env (source that file first, or export it
# yourself) — no separate secret to create or store here.
# Model catalog: packages/dto/src/schemas/zai-models.schema.ts
# STRIX_LLM=openai/glm-4.6
# LLM_API_BASE=https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4
# LLM_API_KEY=${ZAI_API_KEY}

# Applies to either profile
STRIX_REASONING_EFFORT=high
